<title>SENEGAL: Senegal favours Swedish-led bid for telecoms stake.</title>
<headline>Senegal favours Swedish-led bid for telecoms stake.</headline>
<dateline>DAKAR 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senegal's government has decided to offer a Swedish-led consortium a one third stake in its state telecommunications company and discussions to finalise the deal are planned for December, privatisation committee sources said.</p>
<p>Swedish company Telia Overseas heads the consortium which includes American company Walter Group, China Telecommunication Services and Senecom Partners, a locally based company, the sources added on Friday.</p>
</text>
